From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:03:09 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] soc: samsung: gs101-pmu: zuma: allow the modem PCIe PHY's
 isolation register

zuma's PCIe PHY for its first controller (the S5300 modem's) is isolated
through PMU offset 0x3ec4, as stock's pcie@12100000 gives it
(pmu-offset). Its PHY driver releases the isolation and sets bit 10 once
the PHY is configured, so add the register to zuma's PMU regmap, next to
the Wi-Fi PHY's 0x3ec8.

On the Pixel 9a, the modem link's bring-up driver read the register as
0xc0 at boot, 0x1 out of isolation and 0x401 after configuration, and
the link came up at Gen1 x1.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
index 40e26951c..6cf15a30b 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
@@ -344,6 +344,7 @@ const struct exynos_pmu_data gs101_pmu_data = {
 #define ZUMA_HSI0_STATUS		0x2a84
 #define ZUMA_PAD_CTRL_NFC_CLK		0x3e84
 #define ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_UFS		0x3ec0
+#define ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE0		0x3ec4
 #define ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE1		0x3ec8
 
 static const struct regmap_range zuma_pmu_registers[] = {
@@ -360,6 +361,7 @@ static const struct regmap_range zuma_pmu_registers[] = {
 	/* PHY isolation */
 	regmap_reg_range(GS101_PHY_CTRL_USB20, GS101_PHY_CTRL_USB20),
 	regmap_reg_range(ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_UFS, ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_UFS),
+	regmap_reg_range(ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE0, ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE0),
 	regmap_reg_range(ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE1, ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE1),
 	/* a hint TF-A reads, not a status register: see zuma_pmu_regmap_init() */
 	regmap_reg_range(ZUMA_PMU_INFORM0, ZUMA_PMU_INFORM0),
